{"reference":"Jeremiah 39","book":"Jeremiah","chapter":39,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Crisis","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter belongs to Jeremiah’s account of Judah’s transition from Babylonian domination through the earlier deportation and the later siege and destruction of Jerusalem. That larger setting helps distinguish the fall described here from the earlier capture of Jerusalem: Jeremiah 39 focuses on Zedekiah’s final defeat, the destruction of the city, the removal of many survivors, and the changed circumstances for those left behind.","verse_refs":["Jeremiah 39:1-18"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_039_48db7eb32cf19c7794d0a92f"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}